### Rotating Card – CSS + HTML

Below is a minimal example that shows a card (a `div` with some content) that rotates 180 ° around its Y‑axis when you hover over it.  
Feel free to copy‑paste the code into an HTML file and open it in a browser.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card Demo</title>
<style>
/* 1️⃣  Container – keeps the card centered and gives perspective */
.card-wrapper {
  width: 300px;
  height: 200px;
  margin: 50px auto;
  perspective: 800px;          /* creates 3‑D effect for children */
}

/* 2️⃣  The card itself – front & back sides */
.card {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  position: relative;
  transform-style: preserve-3d; /* allows children to be positioned in 3‑D space */
  transition: transform 0.6s ease; /* smooth rotation */
}

/* 3️⃣  Front side – visible by default */
.card .front,
.card .back {
  position: absolute;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  backface-visibility: hidden; /* hides the reverse side when turned */
  border-radius: 12px;
  overflow: hidden;
  box-shadow: 0 4px 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.15);
}

/* 3a️⃣  Front side styling */
.card .front {
  background: #fff;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
  font-size: 1.4rem;
  color: #333;
}

/* 3b️⃣  Back side styling – rotated 180° so it starts hidden */
.card .back {
  background: #f8f8f8;
  transform: rotateY(180deg);
  padding: 20px;
  box-sizing: border-box;
  font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
  font-size: 1rem;
  color: #555;
}

/* 4️⃣  Hover effect – rotate the whole card */
.card:hover {
  transform: rotateY(180deg);
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
  <div class="card">
    <!-- Front side -->
    <div class="front">
      <h2>Front Side</h2>
    </div>

    <!-- Back side -->
    <div class="back">
      <h3>Back Side</h3>
      <p>To zobaczysz, że karta obróci się po najechaniu kursorem.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

#### How it works

| Element | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `.card-wrapper` | Provides a 3‑D perspective for its child. |
| `.card` | Holds the two sides; `transform-style: preserve-3d` lets its children be positioned in 3‑D space. |
| `.front` / `.back` | Each side is absolutely positioned on top of each other. `backface-visibility: hidden` hides the side that is turned away from the viewer. |
| `.back` | Rotated 180° initially so it starts hidden. |
| `.card:hover` | Rotates the whole card 180° around the Y‑axis, revealing the back side. |

You can replace the content inside `.front` and `.back` with images, text, or any other elements you like.  
If you want a different rotation axis (e.g., X‑axis for a flip‑over effect), just change `rotateY` to `rotateX` in the CSS.
